# Terraform for {{ project_name }}

Provisions:

- GCS pipeline root bucket
- Artifact Registry (Cloud Run image)
- Pub/Sub topics + push subscriptions (training / prediction + DLQ)
- Cloud Run trigger service
- Cloud Scheduler cron jobs (schedules in `terraform.tfvars`)
- Cloud Build triggers (PR / push / release) when `github_owner` + `github_repo` are set
- IAM for trigger, scheduler, and Cloud Build service accounts

## Quick start

```bash
# from repo root
make tf-init
make tf-plan
make tf-apply
```

Edit cron schedules and GitHub settings in [`terraform.tfvars`](terraform.tfvars):

```hcl
training_cron   = "{{ training_cron }}"
prediction_cron = "{{ prediction_cron }}"
github_owner    = "your-org"
github_repo     = "{{ project_slug }}"
```

## Bootstrap order

1. `make compile` and upload artifacts (`make publish-artifacts BUCKET=...`) or cut a release tag.
2. Build/push the Cloud Run image (release Cloud Build) so the service has a runnable image.
3. `terraform apply` (or push to `main` once the push trigger exists).

Cloud Build GitHub triggers require the Cloud Build GitHub app connection for `github_owner`/`github_repo`.
